 "marks": [
  {
   "d": "2021-10-28",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY21",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Although we don't have full visibility on future market volumes, the pipeline is encouraging and indicates that revenues in Q4 will be ahead of 2019 levels.",
   "file": "20211028_FOXT_Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-01-27",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY21",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "The Group expects adjusted operating profit in 2021 to be circa £7m, at the top end of market expectations.",
   "file": "20220127_FOXT_Year-End-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-03-02",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "We successfully delivered the first phase of our growth plan, making strong progress against our core strategic objectives and are confident of delivering further growth this year and into the future.",
   "file": "20220302_FOXT_Final-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-04-21",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Commenting on the first quarter, Nic Budden, Chief Executive Officer said: \"I am pleased to report we have had a good start to the year, with all areas of the business trading in line with our expectations.",
   "file": "20220421_FOXT_Q1-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-05-30",
   "doc": "H1 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Foxtons has made a good start to the financial year and current trading remains in line with the Board's expectations.",
   "file": "20220530_FOXT_Foxtons-Appoints-Guy-Gittins-as-Group-CEO.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-07-28",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "Notwithstanding the global and domestic headwinds impacting the UK economy, we expect adjusted earnings growth in the second half compared to H2 2021, including some additional benefit from the recent lettings portfolio acquisitions. We anticipate adjusted earnings for the full year to be at least in line with market expectations.",
   "file": "20220728_FOXT_Half-year-Report.md",
   "gnote": "early signal: first step up in tone"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-10-27",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 2,
   "q": "Accordingly, we now expect to deliver a result for the 2022 financial year ahead of our previous expectations.",
   "file": "20221027_FOXT_Q3-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-01-26",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 2,
   "q": "Lettings, Sales and Financial Services all delivered revenue growth in 2022, with Group revenue ahead of market expectations at c.£140m (up c.11% year-on-year).",
   "file": "20230126_FOXT_UNAUDITED-FY22-YEAR-END-TRADING-UPDATE.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-03-07",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "The overall outlook for 2023 is expected to be more challenging than 2022, due to the highly uncertain macroeconomic backdrop, including significantly higher interest rates and inflation levels than in prior years impacting the sales market.",
   "file": "20230307_FOXT_Final-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-04-20",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "20 April 2023 - Foxtons Group plc (LSE: FOXT) has started the new financial year well and in line with management's expectations.",
   "file": "20230420_FOXT_Q1-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-07-27",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Trading since the end of the first half is in line with our expectations. July 2023 Lettings revenue is performing in line with the trends seen H1 2023, and we continue to deliver strong organic growth.",
   "file": "20230727_FOXT_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-10-26",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Overall, full year earnings are expected to be in-line with consensus7.",
   "file": "20231026_FOXT_Q3-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-01-25",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 2,
   "q": "Adjusted operating profit of c.£14m was also ahead of consensus market expectations (c.£11.8m) and broadly flat against the prior year (2022: £13.9m) as the Group delivers on its growth strategy by decoupling earnings from sales market cycles.",
   "file": "20240125_FOXT_UNAUDITED-2023-YEAR-END-TRADING-UPDATE.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-03-05",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "By leveraging the operational capabilities of the Foxtons Operating Platform, alongside increased levels of contribution as fee earners hired in 2023 mature, the Group is on track to deliver another year of growth in 2024 and to deliver against our £25m to £30m adjusted operating profit target over the medium-term.",
   "file": "20240305_FOXT_Final-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-04-18",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The Group is trading in line with management's expectations.",
   "file": "20240418_FOXT_Q1-2024-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-07-30",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The Group's expectation for the full year remains unchanged and the Group is on-track to deliver its medium-term target of £25m to £30m adjusted operating profit.",
   "file": "20240730_FOXT_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-10-24",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The Group is trading in line with management's expectations, with full year results expected to be in line with consensus2.",
   "file": "20241024_FOXT_Q3-2024-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-01-28",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "RAISE",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "Adjusted operating profit of c.£19m was also ahead of market expectations and up c.33% against the prior year (2023: £14.3m), as higher revenues and operating leverage within the Foxtons business model drove improved adjusted operating profit margins.",
   "file": "20250128_FOXT_UNAUDITED-2024-YEAR-END-TRADING-UPDATE.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-03-05",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The Group remains on track to deliver against the medium-term target of £28 million to £33 million adjusted operating profit, despite £2 million of additional national insurance costs per annum, reflecting the strength of our core operations and diversified revenue streams.",
   "file": "20250305_FOXT_FULL-YEAR-RESULTS-FOR-YEAR-ENDED-31-DECEMBER-2024.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-04-23",
   "doc": "Q1 TU",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "\"Despite ongoing macro volatility, with our market leadership position and resilient business model, I am confident we can drive further growth this year, and deliver long-term value for shareholders, employees, and customers.\"",
   "file": "20250423_FOXT_Q1-2025-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-07-30",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "In contrast, sales market activity is likely to be more subdued than initially anticipated, as borrowing costs have not reduced at the pace initially forecast.",
   "file": "20250730_FOXT_Interim-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-10-23",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Noting the risks above, full year adjusted operating profit is expected to be in the range of £21.5m to £23.2m2 (2024: £21.6m), with the range primarily reflecting uncertainty over the conversion rate of the Sales under-offer pipeline.",
   "file": "20251023_FOXT_Q3-2025-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2026-01-15",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY26",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "Sales began 2026 with a lower under-offer pipeline than the previous year, as a result of the significant sales market disruption around the Autumn Budget and a very strong comparative period in Q4 2024 (ahead of the March 2025 stamp duty deadline).",
   "file": "20260115_FOXT_Unaudited-Year-End-Trading-Update-and-Acquisition.md"
